   "evidence": "Upstream analogue for the same object: `mathlib/Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Measure/CharacteristicFunction/Basic.lean:140` `@[simp] lemma charFun_zero (\u03bc : Measure E) : charFun \u03bc 0 = \u03bc.real Set.univ` \u2014 unconditional; the same file keeps the hypothesis-free `norm_charFun_le` alongside `norm_charFun_le_one` (line 177). `integral_const` is unconditional (`mathlib/Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Integral/Bochner/Basic.lean:987`: `\u222b _ : \u03b1, c \u2202\u03bc = \u03bc.real univ \u2022 c`), so no typeclass is needed.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Nuclear/Medium/Collective/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "State `@[simp] theorem anisotropyCoeff_zero (\u03bc : Measure (AddCircle T)) : anisotropyCoeff \u03bc 0 = \u03bc.real Set.univ` (proof: `simp [anisotropyCoeff]`), and if the value `1` is wanted, derive it as a corollary under `[IsProbabilityMeasure \u03bc]`.",
   "issue": "`anisotropyCoeff_zero` assumes `[IsProbabilityMeasure \u03bc]`, but `anisotropyCoeff \u03bc 0 = \u222b x, fourier 0 x \u2202\u03bc = \u222b x, 1 \u2202\u03bc` is `\u03bc.real Set.univ` for *any* measure. As a `simp` lemma it then fails to fire on exactly the measures the rest of the file handles \u2014 e.g. `haarAddCircle.withDensity f` of `anisotropyCoeff_withDensity` (line 228), which carries no probability instance.",
   "line": "209"
  }
